Black sea bass habitat grew significantly between 1993 and 2023. Both the northern and southern edges of black sea bass distribution shifted northward. Distributions have also expanded eastward along the coast of southern New England (@fig-shifts-bsb). The weighted centroid shifted nearly 12 km north-northeast during this time. 

There is a predicted loss of core black sea bass habitat along the continental shelf break. However, total habitat area is predicted to continue to increase between 2025 and 2035 due to continued northward expansion into the Gulf of Maine and Cape Cod (@fig-shifts-bsb). The weighted centroid is predicted to continue to shift a further 31 km north-northeast.

In the previous Assessment, black sea bass received a High Distributional Vulnerability Rank due to high adult mobility and high dispersal of eggs and larvae [@hare2016vulnerability]. 

